Idea sources
- data-cleaner-agent (MIT): plan-versus-execute ("the model plans, it never touches values"), one
  plan(profile) interface with an offline rule planner beside an LLM planner, and a fixed dispatch
  whitelist. This project rejects unknown operations with reasons instead of skipping them, uses strict
  schemas, and takes a stated date format instead of per-value inference.
- goldenflow (MIT): dry run before apply; manifest records with affected rows and before/after samples,
  which inform the step-card counts and samples. Not a dependency.
- OpenRefine (BSD-3-Clause): operation history, rollback to an earlier step and JSON extract/apply,
  which inform LIFO undo-to-step-N and plan export/import.
- Cocoon (MIT): per-step human feedback on model proposals.
- tab_err (Apache-2.0): separating where errors land from how values are corrupted, which informs the
  seeded-error injector.
- databonsai (MIT): its cell-rewriting behaviour is reproduced as the `llm_direct` comparison baseline
  (behaviour only).
- LLM4DC / AutoDCWorkflow (no licence stated): read for background only; no data or code used.

Deliberately not used: LLM4DC, CleanAgent and AutoDCWorkflow data or code (no licence); Raha benchmark
data is never committed (terms undocumented; the optional download script writes to a gitignored folder);
Jellyfish (CC BY-NC); open expression languages (GREL, regex) and code generation.
